      <p>You might want to remove a hosted cluster if you are no longer using it, you are trying to reduce resources, or the hosted cluster is experiencing issues that are difficult to resolve.</p>
      <h2 id="destroy-hc-bm-cli_hcp-destroy-bm" class="group scroll-mt-20">Destroying a hosted cluster on bare metal by using the CLI<a href="#destroy-hc-bm-cli_hcp-destroy-bm" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">If you created a hosted cluster by using the command-line interface (CLI), you can destroy that hosted cluster and its back-end resources by running a command.</p>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>
      Delete the hosted cluster and its back-end resources by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc delete -f <hosted_cluster_config>.yaml"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>Specify the name of the configuration YAML file that was rendered when you created the hosted cluster.</p>
      <Alert variant="note" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Note</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>If you created the hosted cluster without specifying the <code>--render</code> and <code>--render-sensitive</code> flags in its configuration file, you must remove its back-end resources manually.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      </li>
      </ul>
      <h2 id="destroy-hc-bm-console_hcp-destroy-bm" class="group scroll-mt-20">Destroying a hosted cluster on bare metal by using the web console<a href="#destroy-hc-bm-console_hcp-destroy-bm" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">You can use the multicluster engine Operator web console to destroy a hosted cluster on bare metal.</p>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>In the console, click <strong>Infrastructure</strong> -&gt; <strong>Clusters</strong>.</li>
